# chatter: chat sessions told with source "chat" (user turns only, as an MCP client relays them). A task only for the user's own commitment; off-topic chat (coding help, a recipe, an assistant's advice, a friend's task) makes none. All cases are fictional, written to read like real chats; noise-coding is the kind of long coding chat that once made two tasks. Runs the REAL tiers: `ken eval reconcile evals/chatter.jsonl`.
{"id": "real-plumber", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: Quick update on the kitchen. I need to call Tomas the plumber on Friday to confirm the start date.", "expect": {"must": {"add_task": ["task", "task_exists", "pending"]}}}
{"id": "real-invoice", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: I promised Priya I'd send her the signed contractor invoice by Wednesday, so that's on me.", "expect": {"must": {"add_task": ["task", "task_exists", "pending"]}}}
{"id": "real-book-flights", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: We settled on Lisbon for the May trip. I'll book the flights this weekend before prices go up.", "expect": {"must": {"add_task": ["task", "task_exists", "pending"]}}}
{"id": "real-accept-request", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: Marco asked me to review the launch deck before Thursday's meeting and I said yes, I'll do it tomorrow morning.", "expect": {"must": {"add_task": ["task", "task_exists", "pending"]}}}
{"id": "noise-coding", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: I’ve got a weird Python bug at work. The filter returns no rows, but I can see matching records in the input. User: ```python for row in records: if row.get(\"status\") == \"active\": results.append(row) ``` The input comes from a CSV. User: Oh, I printed it. It says `' active'` with a space before it. Didn’t notice that. User: That fixed the filter, but now I get `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'strip'` on a few rows. User: Makes sense. I also have a test that still fails because it expects 3 results and gets 2. User: `active`, ` active `, and `enabled`. I guess enabled was never supposed to count as active. User: Yep, 2 is correct. I’ll update the fixture expectation and add a whitespace case.", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task"]}}
{"id": "noise-recipe", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: What's a good weeknight recipe with chickpeas and spinach? User: Could I use coconut milk instead of cream? User: Nice, how long should it simmer?", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task"]}}
{"id": "noise-advice", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: How should a launch plan usually be structured? User: So your advice is: clean it up, add owners and dates for each section, and send it around to the team for comments? User: Makes sense, good general advice.", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task"]}}
{"id": "noise-friend", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: My friend Dana is stressed, she has to finish her thesis chapter and email it to her advisor by Monday. User: What could she do to focus better?", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task"]}}
{"id": "noise-running", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: I want to start running again but I'm out of shape, I can jog about 5 minutes. User: A run-walk plan three times a week sounds doable. User: Ok so 1 minute jog, 2 minutes walk, 8 rounds. Nice.", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task", "remember_fact", "remember_preference"]}}
{"id": "noise-phone-choice", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: Help me compare the Pixel 10 and the iPhone 17. I record a lot of video and hate phones that get hot. User: Hm, I still lean toward the Pixel for the camera. Not buying yet though.", "expect": {"must_not": ["add_task", "remember_fact", "remember_preference"]}}
